IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P9-gate`
IMPORT `aia-scope`

-- P9-art-100-101: Article 100 "Administrative fines on Union institutions, bodies, offices and agencies" (group of Articles 99 and 100,
-- 2 August 2025) and Article 101 "Fines for providers of general-purpose AI models" (the group General, 2 August 2026, Article 113(b) excepts it).
-- Both are unchanged by the Omnibus. Every function takes `the date asked` first; before the group applies the answer is NOTHING.
-- The European Data Protection Supervisor and the Commission are officials: no seat. A Union institution, body, office or agency is a
-- deployer for the deployer seat; the provider of a general-purpose AI model is the gpai seat. Money is a NUMBER of euros.
-- Split site (i): "Non-compliance with ... shall be subject to administrative fines" (Article 100(2), (3)) answers NOTHING when the
-- non-compliance is not established (no "where", "if" or "only"): forks F-100-2 and F-100-3.
-- Split site (ii): the "may" of Article 101(1) is gated by "when the Commission finds that ...": JUST FALSE per ruling (b), fork F-101-1.
-- The text says "The Commission shall also into account commitments": read as "shall also take into account", fork F-101-1-typo.

§ `Seam S14: the reference this Article gives to Article 2(2)`

-- Article 2(2): for a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in
-- Section B of Annex I, "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply". The keel asks of a provision by its Article
-- number, letter and paragraph; paragraph 0 means the whole Article.

`Art 100 reference to the provision` MEANS `Article reference` WITH
    number IS 100
    letter IS ""
    paragraph IS 0

§ `Article 100: the parties, the acts and the infringements`

DECLARE `Art 100 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 100 the European Data Protection Supervisor`

DECLARE `Art 100 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 100(4) give the Union institution, body, office or agency the opportunity of being heard on the matter regarding the possible infringement`
    `Art 100(7) notify the Commission of the administrative fines imposed and of any litigation or judicial proceedings initiated`

DECLARE `Art 100 infringement` IS ONE OF
    `Art 100(2) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5`
    `Art 100(3) the non-compliance of the AI system with a requirement or obligation under this Regulation other than those laid down in Article 5`
    `Art 100 another infringement`

DECLARE `Art 100(1) factor` IS ONE OF
    `Art 100(1)(a) the nature, gravity and duration of the infringement and of its consequences, taking into account the purpose of the AI system concerned, as well as, where appropriate, the number of affected persons and the level of damage suffered by them`
    `Art 100(1)(b) the degree of responsibility of the Union institution, body, office or agency, taking into account technical and organisational measures implemented by them`
    `Art 100(1)(c) any action taken by the Union institution, body, office or agency to mitigate the damage suffered by affected persons`
    `Art 100(1)(d) the degree of cooperation with the European Data Protection Supervisor in order to remedy the infringement and mitigate the possible adverse effects of the infringement`
    `Art 100(1)(e) any similar previous infringements by the Union institution, body, office or agency`
    `Art 100(1)(f) the manner in which the infringement became known to the European Data Protection Supervisor, in particular whether, and if so to what extent, the Union institution, body, office or agency notified the infringement`
    `Art 100(1)(g) the annual budget of the Union institution, body, office or agency`
    `Art 100(1) another factor`

-- src:1510 | 1. The European Data Protection Supervisor may impose administrative fines on Union institutions, bodies, offices and agencies falling within the scope of this Regulation. When deciding whether to impose an administrative fine and when deciding on the amount of the administrative fine in each individual case, all relevant circumstances of the specific situation shall be taken into account and due regard shall be given to the following:
@ref Art 100(1) (src:1510)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the body is a Union institution, body, office or agency falling within the scope of this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 100(1) the European Data Protection Supervisor may impose administrative fines on the body` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that the Regulation gives no such power
    ELSE IF `the body is a Union institution, body, office or agency falling within the scope of this Regulation`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is over "Union institutions, bodies, offices and agencies falling within the scope of this Regulation"; for another body it is silent

-- src:1511 | (a) the nature, gravity and duration of the infringement and of its consequences, taking into account the purpose of the AI system concerned, as well as, where appropriate, the number of affected persons and the level of damage suffered by them;
-- src:1512 | (b) the degree of responsibility of the Union institution, body, office or agency, taking into account technical and organisational measures implemented by them;
-- src:1513 | (c) any action taken by the Union institution, body, office or agency to mitigate the damage suffered by affected persons;
-- src:1514 | (d) the degree of cooperation with the European Data Protection Supervisor in order to remedy the infringement and mitigate the possible adverse effects of the infringement, including compliance with any of the measures previously ordered by the European Data Protection Supervisor against the Union institution, body, office or agency concerned with regard to the same subject matter;
-- src:1515 | (e) any similar previous infringements by the Union institution, body, office or agency;
-- src:1516 | (f) the manner in which the infringement became known to the European Data Protection Supervisor, in particular whether, and if so to what extent, the Union institution, body, office or agency notified the infringement;
-- src:1517 | (g) the annual budget of the Union institution, body, office or agency.
@ref Art 100(1) points (a) to (g) (src:1511-1517)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the European Data Protection Supervisor is deciding whether to impose an administrative fine or on its amount` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the factor` IS AN `Art 100(1) factor`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 100(1) due regard must be given to the factor` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF NOT `the European Data Protection Supervisor is deciding whether to impose an administrative fine or on its amount`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the factors are for "when deciding whether to impose an administrative fine and when deciding on the amount"
         ELSE CONSIDER `the factor`
              WHEN `Art 100(1) another factor` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "due regard shall be given to the following" names points (a) to (g); other relevant circumstances are taken into account under the first part of the paragraph
              OTHERWISE JUST TRUE  -- "due regard shall be given": no "as appropriate" gate, unlike Article 99(7)

-- Paragraphs 2 and 3: EUR 1 500 000 for Article 5, EUR 750 000 for any other requirement or obligation.
-- src:1518 | 2. Non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5 shall be subject to administrative fines of up to EUR 1 500 000 .
-- src:1519 | 3. The non-compliance of the AI system with any requirements or obligations under this Regulation, other than those laid down in Article 5, shall be subject to administrative fines of up to EUR 750 000 .
@ref Art 100(2) and (3) (src:1518-1519)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the infringement` IS AN `Art 100 infringement`
      `the non-compliance is established` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 100 the non-compliance of the body is subject to administrative fines` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF `Art 2(2) the provision applies to the high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `Art 100 reference to the provision` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) as amended: "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" (as enacted: "only Article 6(1), Articles 102 to 109 and Article 112 apply"); this provision is not among them (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
         ELSE CONSIDER `the infringement`
              WHEN `Art 100 another infringement` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): no paragraph names a fine for it
              OTHERWISE
                  IF `the non-compliance is established`
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Non-compliance with ... shall be subject to administrative fines": the sentence is about non-compliance and has no "where", "if" or "only" (split site (i): fork F-100-2, F-100-3)

@ref Art 100(2) and (3)
GIVEN `the infringement` IS AN `Art 100 infringement`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Art 100 the ceiling in euros of the administrative fine on the body` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the infringement`
    WHEN `Art 100(2) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` THEN JUST 1500000
    WHEN `Art 100(3) the non-compliance of the AI system with a requirement or obligation under this Regulation other than those laid down in Article 5` THEN JUST 750000
    WHEN `Art 100 another infringement` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no paragraph states a ceiling for it

-- src:1520 | 4. Before taking decisions pursuant to this Article, the European Data Protection Supervisor shall give the Union institution, body, office or agency which is the subject of the proceedings conducted by the European Data Protection Supervisor the opportunity of being heard on the matter regarding the possible infringement. The European Data Protection Supervisor shall base his or her decisions only on elements and circumstances on which the parties concerned have been able to comment. Complainants, if any, shall be associated closely with the proceedings.
@ref Art 100(4) (src:1520)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the European Data Protection Supervisor is about to take a decision pursuant to Article 100` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 100(4) the European Data Protection Supervisor must give the body the opportunity of being heard` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF `the European Data Protection Supervisor is about to take a decision pursuant to Article 100`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is "before taking decisions pursuant to this Article", which arises only when a decision is to be taken

@ref Art 100(4)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the European Data Protection Supervisor is about to take a decision pursuant to Article 100` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 100 party` `Art 100 act`
`Art 100(4) the duty of the European Data Protection Supervisor to give the body the opportunity of being heard` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 100(4) the European Data Protection Supervisor must give the body the opportunity of being heard` `the date asked` `the European Data Protection Supervisor is about to take a decision pursuant to Article 100`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY `Art 100 the European Data Protection Supervisor`
        MUST `Art 100(4) give the Union institution, body, office or agency the opportunity of being heard on the matter regarding the possible infringement`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

@ref Art 100(4)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the parties concerned have been able to comment on the element or circumstance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 100(4) the decision may be based on the element or circumstance` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is required
    ELSE IF `the parties concerned have been able to comment on the element or circumstance`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The European Data Protection Supervisor shall base his or her decisions only on elements and circumstances on which the parties concerned have been able to comment" (a list closed with "only")

@ref Art 100(4)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `there is a complainant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 100(4) complainants must be associated closely with the proceedings` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF `there is a complainant`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Complainants, if any, shall be associated closely": without a complainant the sentence is silent

-- src:1521 | 5. The rights of defence of the parties concerned shall be fully respected in the proceedings. They shall be entitled to have access to the European Data Protection Supervisor’s file, subject to the legitimate interest of individuals or undertakings in the protection of their personal data or business secrets.
@ref Art 100(5) (src:1521)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `proceedings are conducted by the European Data Protection Supervisor under this Article` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 100(5) the rights of defence of the parties concerned must be fully respected` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF `proceedings are conducted by the European Data Protection Supervisor under this Article`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "the proceedings" of this Article

@ref Art 100(5)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the party is a party concerned in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `access would infringe the legitimate interest of individuals or undertakings in the protection of their personal data or business secrets` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 100(5) the party concerned is entitled to have access to the file of the European Data Protection Supervisor` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that the Regulation gives no such entitlement
    ELSE IF NOT `the party is a party concerned in the proceedings`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the entitlement is of "the parties concerned"
         ELSE IF `access would infringe the legitimate interest of individuals or undertakings in the protection of their personal data or business secrets`
              THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to the legitimate interest of individuals or undertakings in the protection of their personal data or business secrets": the entitlement is limited, and the text does not say whether the limit denies access to the whole file (an "entitled" function: fork F-100-5)
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1522 | 6. Funds collected by imposition of fines in this Article shall contribute to the general budget of the Union. The fines shall not affect the effective operation of the Union institution, body, office or agency fined.
@ref Art 100(6) (src:1522)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `a fine is imposed under this Article` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 100(6) the funds collected by the fine contribute to the general budget of the Union` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is stated
    ELSE IF `a fine is imposed under this Article`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "funds collected by imposition of fines in this Article"

@ref Art 100(6)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `a fine is imposed under this Article` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 100(6) the fine may affect the effective operation of the body fined` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is stated
    ELSE IF `a fine is imposed under this Article`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The fines shall not affect the effective operation of the Union institution, body, office or agency fined" (a flat negative)
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "the fines" imposed under this Article

-- src:1523 | 7. The European Data Protection Supervisor shall, on an annual basis, notify the Commission of the administrative fines it has imposed pursuant to this Article and of any litigation or judicial proceedings it has initiated.
@ref Art 100(7) (src:1523)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `administrative fines were imposed or litigation or judicial proceedings were initiated during the year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 100(7) the European Data Protection Supervisor must notify the Commission on an annual basis` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF `administrative fines were imposed or litigation or judicial proceedings were initiated during the year`
         THEN JUST TRUE  -- "on an annual basis": the text gives no date by which the notification is due
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the notification is "of the administrative fines it has imposed ... and of any litigation or judicial proceedings it has initiated"; when there are none the sentence is silent

@ref Art 100(7)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `administrative fines were imposed or litigation or judicial proceedings were initiated during the year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 100 party` `Art 100 act`
`Art 100(7) the duty of the European Data Protection Supervisor to notify the Commission on an annual basis` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 100(7) the European Data Protection Supervisor must notify the Commission on an annual basis` `the date asked` `administrative fines were imposed or litigation or judicial proceedings were initiated during the year`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY `Art 100 the European Data Protection Supervisor`
        MUST `Art 100(7) notify the Commission of the administrative fines imposed and of any litigation or judicial proceedings initiated`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

§ `Article 101: fines for providers of general-purpose AI models`

DECLARE `Art 101 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 101 the Commission`

DECLARE `Art 101 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 101(2) communicate its preliminary findings to the provider of the general-purpose AI model and give it an opportunity to be heard`
    `Art 101(4) communicate information on the fines imposed to the Board`
    `Art 101(6) adopt implementing acts containing detailed arrangements and procedural safeguards for proceedings`

DECLARE `Art 101(1) factor` IS ONE OF
    `Art 101(1) the nature, gravity and duration of the infringement`
    `Art 101(1) the principles of proportionality and appropriateness`
    `Art 101(1) commitments made in accordance with Article 93(3)`
    `Art 101(1) commitments made in relevant codes of practice in accordance with Article 56`
    `Art 101(1) another factor`

-- src:1526 | 1. The Commission may impose on providers of general-purpose AI models fines not exceeding 3 % of their annual total worldwide turnover in the preceding financial year or EUR 15 000 000 , whichever is higher., when the Commission finds that the provider intentionally or negligently:
-- src:1527 | (a) infringed the relevant provisions of this Regulation;
-- src:1528 | (b) failed to comply with a request for a document or for information pursuant to Article 91, or supplied incorrect, incomplete or misleading information;
-- src:1529 | (c) failed to comply with a measure requested under Article 93;
-- src:1530 | (d) failed to make available to the Commission access to the general-purpose AI model or general-purpose AI model with systemic risk with a view to conducting an evaluation pursuant to Article 92.
@ref Art 101(1) (src:1526-1530)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission finds that the provider acted intentionally or negligently` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider infringed the relevant provisions of this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider failed to comply with a request for a document or for information pursuant to Article 91, or supplied incorrect, incomplete or misleading information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider failed to comply with a measure requested under Article 93` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider failed to make available to the Commission access to the model with a view to conducting an evaluation pursuant to Article 92` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 101(1) the Commission may impose a fine on the provider of the general-purpose AI model` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that the Regulation gives no such power
    ELSE IF       `the Commission finds that the provider acted intentionally or negligently`
              AND (   `the provider infringed the relevant provisions of this Regulation`
                   OR `the provider failed to comply with a request for a document or for information pursuant to Article 91, or supplied incorrect, incomplete or misleading information`
                   OR `the provider failed to comply with a measure requested under Article 93`
                   OR `the provider failed to make available to the Commission access to the model with a view to conducting an evaluation pursuant to Article 92`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Commission may impose on providers of general-purpose AI models fines ..., when the Commission finds that the provider intentionally or negligently: (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; (d) ..." (a "when" gate on a "may": split site (ii), fork F-101-1)

-- "not exceeding 3 % of their annual total worldwide turnover in the preceding financial year or EUR 15 000 000, whichever is higher"
@ref Art 101(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the total worldwide annual turnover of the provider for the preceding financial year in euros` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Art 101(1) the ceiling in euros of the fine on the provider` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that no ceiling is stated
    ELSE JUST (IF 15000000 AT LEAST (`the total worldwide annual turnover of the provider for the preceding financial year in euros` TIMES 3 DIVIDED BY 100) THEN 15000000 ELSE (`the total worldwide annual turnover of the provider for the preceding financial year in euros` TIMES 3 DIVIDED BY 100))  -- "whichever is higher"

-- src:1531 | In fixing the amount of the fine or periodic penalty payment, regard shall be had to the nature, gravity and duration of the infringement, taking due account of the principles of proportionality and appropriateness. The Commission shall also into account commitments made in accordance with Article 93(3) or made in relevant codes of practice in accordance with Article 56.
@ref Art 101(1) second subparagraph (src:1531)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission is fixing the amount of the fine or periodic penalty payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the factor` IS AN `Art 101(1) factor`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 101(1) regard must be had to the factor in fixing the amount` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF NOT `the Commission is fixing the amount of the fine or periodic penalty payment`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "fixing the amount of the fine or periodic penalty payment"
         ELSE CONSIDER `the factor`
              WHEN `Art 101(1) another factor` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sentence names the nature, gravity and duration, the principles of proportionality and appropriateness, and the commitments, and does not say "only"
              OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1532 | 2. Before adopting the decision pursuant to paragraph 1, the Commission shall communicate its preliminary findings to the provider of the general-purpose AI model and give it an opportunity to be heard.
@ref Art 101(2) (src:1532)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission is about to adopt a decision pursuant to paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 101(2) the Commission must communicate its preliminary findings to the provider and give it an opportunity to be heard` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF `the Commission is about to adopt a decision pursuant to paragraph 1`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is "before adopting the decision pursuant to paragraph 1", which arises only when a decision is to be adopted

@ref Art 101(2)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission is about to adopt a decision pursuant to paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 101 party` `Art 101 act`
`Art 101(2) the duty of the Commission to communicate its preliminary findings to the provider and give it an opportunity to be heard` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 101(2) the Commission must communicate its preliminary findings to the provider and give it an opportunity to be heard` `the date asked` `the Commission is about to adopt a decision pursuant to paragraph 1`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY `Art 101 the Commission`
        MUST `Art 101(2) communicate its preliminary findings to the provider of the general-purpose AI model and give it an opportunity to be heard`
