    ELSE IF NOT `a fine has been imposed under this Article`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "fines imposed under this Article"
         ELSE IF `it is appropriate to communicate the information to the Board`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Information on fines imposed under this Article shall also be communicated to the Board as appropriate" (an "as appropriate" gate on a duty that is not met: fork F-101-4)

@ref Art 101(4)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `a fine has been imposed under this Article` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate to communicate the information to the Board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 101 party` `Art 101 act`
`Art 101(4) the duty of the Commission to communicate the information on the fines imposed to the Board` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 101(4) the Commission must communicate the information on the fines imposed to the Board` `the date asked` `a fine has been imposed under this Article` `it is appropriate to communicate the information to the Board`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY `Art 101 the Commission`
        MUST `Art 101(4) communicate information on the fines imposed to the Board`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

-- "The Court of Justice of the European Union shall have unlimited jurisdiction to review decisions of the Commission fixing a fine under this Article."
DECLARE `Art 101(5) outcome` IS ONE OF
    `Art 101(5) cancel the fine imposed`
    `Art 101(5) reduce the fine imposed`
    `Art 101(5) increase the fine imposed`
    `Art 101(5) another outcome`

-- src:1535 | 5. The Court of Justice of the European Union shall have unlimited jurisdiction to review decisions of the Commission fixing a fine under this Article. It may cancel, reduce or increase the fine imposed.
@ref Art 101(5) (src:1535)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the decision of the Commission fixes a fine under this Article` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 101(5) the Court of Justice has unlimited jurisdiction to review the decision` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that the Regulation gives no such jurisdiction
    ELSE IF `the decision of the Commission fixes a fine under this Article`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the jurisdiction is over "decisions of the Commission fixing a fine under this Article"; for another decision it is silent

@ref Art 101(5)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the decision of the Commission fixes a fine under this Article` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the outcome` IS AN `Art 101(5) outcome`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 101(5) the Court of Justice may reach the outcome on the fine imposed` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that the Regulation gives no such power
    ELSE IF NOT `the decision of the Commission fixes a fine under this Article`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "the fine imposed" under this Article
         ELSE CONSIDER `the outcome`
              WHEN `Art 101(5) another outcome` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "unlimited jurisdiction" and "It may cancel, reduce or increase the fine imposed": the sentence names three outcomes and does not say "only"
              OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1536 | 6. The Commission shall adopt implementing acts containing detailed arrangements and procedural safeguards for proceedings in view of the possible adoption of decisions pursuant to paragraph 1 of this Article. Those implementing acts shall be adopted in accordance with the examination procedure referred to in Article 98(2).
@ref Art 101(6) (src:1536)
